<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Hui Shung buys 54,000T soybean at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Hui Shung buys 54,000T soybean at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Hui Shung Group bought a shipment of 54,000 tonnes of U.S. soybeans from Cargill at a tender on Thursday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The shipment was bought on a basis of cost-and-freight over November Chicago futures, traders said.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p>			U.S. Gulf     Pacific N.W. Price/Futures</p>
<p> Soybeans 54,000  Sep 21-Oct 5  Sep 16-30    120.75/Nov</p>
<p>The Hui Shung Group includes Hui Shung Agriculture and Food Corp, Eagle Food Industry and Charoen Pokphand.</p>
<p>-- George Hsu, Taipei newsroom (8862-5080815)</p>
</text>
